  "prefLabel": "Per 102.26 “Compensatory time” refers to the practice of offering time off to an employee instead of payment",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Per 102.26 “Compensatory time” refers to the practice of offering time off to an employee instead of payment. Instead of receiving additional pay for the extra time worked, the employee receives equivalent time off at a later date.\n\nSource. #14434, eff 12-1-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/per100-1500.html"
